  "response_text": "The set PSP function is what physically defines where the thread\u2019s stack is located. The Process Stack Pointer is where in memory the running thread exists. Once initialized, it can access that memory based on the PSP location. In the event where PSP is not pointing to the thread stack, then the CPU would be accessing memory from different memory locations. This leads to a hard fault since those locations are not initialized or invalid addresses, since they are not what was set for this thread.\\n",
